I agree with these ideas. In addition, while kittens/cats (but not large cats)
should have less bite damage then dogs, they should also have two claw attacks
with the possibility of blinding. They should also have jumping ability similar
in effect to when a player has it, as well as heightened vision in the dark
(perhaps equivalent to the next outer perimeter of 16 spaces) whenever vision
is used in determining pet actions. IMHO, these features will make cats 
desirable companions, even though they would be unwilling to steal for you.

If anyone questions the realism of a cat protecting its master, I would like
to point out that, in real life, cats have saved the lives of their owners in
situations where they could easily abandoned them for their own safety- 
perhaps not to the extent where they would _attack_ someone (or thing) else,
but then, we _are_ talking about a game here...:)
   
